cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this work, please cite it as below."
title: "A Noise-Invariant Determinism Theorem for Multi-Base Post-Processing in Shor's Order Finding"
abstract: >-
  Five theorems on classical post-processing of multi-base order-finding
  measurements in Shor's algorithm: noise-invariant determinism (T1),
  logarithmic coverage time (T2), exact noise scaling 1/g_M(η) (T3),
  conditional compatibility with Regev's 2023 multi-base framework (T4),
  and a hybrid (C) + Regev b-trick factoring algorithm (T5) with closed-form
  bound matching empirical mean within 4%. Verified across 17,700 measurements
  at six composite sizes. Additionally documents a small (~1-3%) phase-noise-
  induced reduction in run count at sub-Regev-optimal d — a weak instance of
  stochastic resonance under an "anti-optimization" regime.
authors:
